  "final_answer": "I found the answer from WolframAlpha. The page shows the calculation using the Karvonen heart rate reserve formula.\n\n## Answer\n\n**Heart Rate Reserve ≈ 110 bpm (beats per minute)** = 1.833 beats/second\n\n### Details from WolframAlpha:\n- **Inputs used:**\n  - Resting heart rate: 60 bpm\n  - Sex: male\n  - Age: 50 years\n\n- **Formula applied:** Karvonen heart rate reserve formula\n  - HRR = HRmax − HRrest\n  - HRmax = 220 − age = 220 − 50 = 170 bpm\n  - HRR = 170 − 60 = **110 bpm**\n\nThe approximate Heart Rate Reserve for a 50-year-old man with a resting heart rate of 60 bpm is **110 bpm**.",
